This product is inspired by PrivateBin (https://privatebin.info/),
an open-source zero-knowledge pastebin licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

ZeroBin is a clean-room reimplementation. The backend API is written from
scratch in TypeScript for Cloudflare Workers. The frontend is built from
scratch using Svelte and Tailwind CSS. No code from PrivateBin was copied
or modified — only the encryption protocol specification (AES-256-GCM with
PBKDF2 key derivation) was reimplemented for API compatibility.

The encryption protocol used by ZeroBin is based on the PrivateBin v2
format specification, which defines:
- AES-256-GCM symmetric encryption
- PBKDF2-SHA256 key derivation (100,000 iterations)
- Base58 key encoding in URL fragments
- zlib compression of plaintext before encryption

Third-party dependencies are listed in package.json files and are subject
to their own licenses.
